Third-party notices for Hoverdock
=================================

LibreHardwareMonitor (Intel CPU package temperature algorithm)
--------------------------------------------------------------
Portions of the native Intel package-temperature path in src/SystemTemps.cpp
follow the MSR usage in LibreHardwareMonitor's IntelCpu (IA32_TEMPERATURE_TARGET,
IA32_PACKAGE_THERM_STATUS, TjMax - digital readout).

  https://github.com/LibreHardwareMonitor/LibreHardwareMonitor
  License: Mozilla Public License 2.0 / Apache License 2.0

PawnIO IntelMSR module (third_party/pawnio/IntelMSR.bin)
--------------------------------------------------------
Signed PawnIO AMX blob used to read whitelisted Intel MSRs via the PawnIO
kernel driver (\\?\GLOBALROOT\Device\PawnIO). Redistributed from the
LibreHardwareMonitorLib resources / namazso PawnIO.Modules releases.

  https://github.com/namazso/PawnIO.Modules
  https://pawnio.eu/
  License: GNU LGPL 2.1 (see third_party/pawnio/COPYING)

The PawnIO driver itself is a separate system install (not bundled with
Hoverdock). Opening the device typically requires an elevated process on
Windows; Hoverdock uses a one-time elevated scheduled task that runs
Dock.exe --cpu-sensor (same binary, no .NET helper).
